\ `core`: the `no_std` bottom layer of the standard library. `lib/` is not
\ itself a package -- `lib/hosted/` is a sibling package one layer up.
\ `bool` and `cmp` are the typed core the compiler used to inject; `prelude`
\ is the hub that re-exports both, so a consumer spends one `import:` line
\ on the typed surface instead of one per module.
package: core ;
layer: core ;
module: bool cmp prelude combinators option result ;
